<section class="usecases" aria-labelledby="usecases-title">
<div class="uc-top">
<h2 id="usecases-title">Use cases for the sites you run</h2>
<p class="uc-lead">One connected system for facilities, assets, and the teams on site.</p>
<div class="uc-nav">
<button class="uc-prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous stories">←</button>
<button class="uc-next" type="button" aria-label="Next stories">→</button>
</div>
</div>
<div class="uc-row">
<article class="uc-card">
<h3><span class="uc-p">50,000+</span> assets traced. A full audit<br>now takes <span class="uc-g">30 minutes.</span></h3>
<ul class="uc-points">
<li>The only record was the finance system, built from purchase orders and invoices, not from what was on the ground.</li>
<li>An on-site check found ghost assets, duplicate invoices, and equipment that had never been recorded.</li>
<li>Every asset was mapped to one purchase order and invoice, then tagged with RFID.</li>
<li>A handheld reader now sweeps the register in one pass, and warehouse rent is 60% lower.</li>
</ul>
<dl class="uc-stats">
<div><dt class="uc-p">50,000+</dt><dd>assets digitized and RFID-tagged</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-g">30 min</dt><dd>full audit, down from 15 days</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-p">60%</dt><dd>lower warehouse rental</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-g">4,120</dt><dd>ghost assets removed from the books</dd></div>
</dl>
<a class="uc-more" href="/stories/asset-management">Read the full case study →</a>
</article>
<article class="uc-card">
<h3><span class="uc-p">14 campuses.</span> One way of working,<br>and more of the <span class="uc-g">power cost recovered.</span></h3>
<ul class="uc-points">
<li>Each campus had its own cleaning routine, and almost half of planned maintenance was late or missed.</li>
<li>Breakdowns were often fixed locally, with the central team never told.</li>
<li>Meter readings were on paper, so tenant power used after hours was never billed.</li>
<li>FusionEdge put the same SOPs, asset history, and timed readings on every campus.</li>
</ul>
<dl class="uc-stats">
<div><dt class="uc-p">96%</dt><dd>PPM tasks done on time, up from 52%</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-g">45%</dt><dd>fewer unplanned breakdowns</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-p">18%</dt><dd>more electricity cost recovered</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-g">5 days</dt><dd>to set up a new campus, down from 3 weeks</dd></div>
</dl>
<a class="uc-more" href="/stories/facility-operations">Read the full case study →</a>
</article>
<article class="uc-card">
<h3>Pantry orders that took <span class="uc-p">22 minutes</span><br>now arrive in <span class="uc-g">8.</span></h3>
<ul class="uc-points">
<li>More than 300 orders a day came in by phone, and almost a third arrived late.</li>
<li>Nobody could see which order was waiting, so complaints went straight to senior managers.</li>
<li>A QR code at each pantry and meeting room replaced the call. No app to download.</li>
<li>Late orders escalate on their own, and each room level shows its own menu.</li>
</ul>
<dl class="uc-stats">
<div><dt class="uc-p">8 min</dt><dd>average delivery, down from 22 minutes</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-g">97%</dt><dd>orders delivered on time, up from 68%</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-p">92%</dt><dd>fewer escalations to management</dd></div>
<div><dt class="uc-g">4.6</dt><dd>employee satisfaction, up from 3.1 out of 5</dd></div>
</dl>
<a class="uc-more" href="/stories/pantry">Read the full case study →</a>
</article>
</div>
